  localized_key: 
  text: The nurse's office smells like bandaids and old apples. She lets you lie
    on the tiny couch, the one where kids go when they puke or cry. You press your
    cheek to the crinkly paper and whisper, "go away, please, go away," to the voices.
    But they don't.
