  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6b40beeb965e5d9419bf817d6f7d59bb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  go_to_next_node: 1
  executed_from_load: 0
  actor_name_from: 0
  actor: 
  speaker_name_from: 0
  textbox_title: 
  fetch_localized_stat_value: 0
  dialogue_from: 0
  localized_key: 
  text: Integration is the next, most terrifying step. It's not a battle; it's negotiation, 
    reconciliation. You learn that each part, each voice, was created for a reason.
    The rage protected you when you were too small to be angry. The fear held the
    memory so you could function. The child held the capacity for joy so it wouldn't
    be extinguished. Your job is not to evict them, but to thank them. To tell them,
    with a conviction you must slowly build, "your job is done. I am strong enough
    now. I can carry this. You can come home."
  talking_beeps: {fileID: 0}
  darken_all_other_characters: 1
  bring_speaker_to_front: 1
  clear_text_after: 0
  log_text: 1
  log_category: Default
  done_printing: 0
  no_voice_playing: 0
  done_voice_clip: 0
